<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Darangen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Darangen is the epic of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranao-people">Maranao people</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-lanao">Lake Lanao</a> region on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindanao">Mindanao</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. Its long cycles of chanted verse tell of the hero Bantugan and other heroes, preserving Maranao history, customary law, values and aesthetics. It was traditionally performed at weddings and other celebrations over several nights, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> recognised it as part of the intangible cultural heritage of humanity.</p></div>
